33
# Commits in the FULL history that name the tooling or link a private session.
# Measured 2026-08-11 by two independent implementations that agree: the bash gate
# and a python cross-check, 33 of 161.
#
# NOT a target and NOT an acceptance: a RATCHET. The gate fails when this number
# GROWS. It does not fail on the existing 33, because cleaning them needs a history
# rewrite and a force push — that destroys every other clone and is Ivan's
# decision, not a gate's.
#
# WHAT THE 33 ARE: the harness's default commit convention appends
# `Co-Authored-By: Claude <model>` and `Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/...`
# to every commit unless something stops it. Nothing stopped it. The standing rule
# — no tooling names in public history — lived in memory, and a rule in memory
# competes with a default that fires automatically.
#
# WHY FULL HISTORY AND NOT A WINDOW: with a fixed depth, clean commits push old
# dirty ones out of the window and the count falls on its own, so the ratchet would
# report "the leak shrank" for a history that never changed.
#
# When history is cleaned, set this to the new count. The gate says so explicitly
# when it sees the number fall.
